Linux kernel built with the Sys V IPC support(CONFGI_SYSVIPC) is vulnerable to a use-after-free flaw caused by a race condition during deletion of a shared memory file object. It could occur while using shmctl(IPC_RMID) along with other shm system calls. A user/program could use this flaw to crash a system resulting in DoS. Upstream fix: ------------- -> https://git.kernel.org/linus/a399b29dfbaaaf91162b2dc5a5875dd51bbfa2a1
