patch code
=============================================
Linux kernel built with the Sys V IPC support(CONFGI_SYSVIPC) is vulnerable to a use-after-free flaw caused by a race condition during deletion of a shared memory file object. It could occur while using shmctl(IPC_RMID) along with other shm system calls. A user/program could use this flaw to crash a system resulting in DoS. Upstream fix: ------------- -> https://git.kernel.org/linus/a399b29dfbaaaf91162b2dc5a5875dd51bbfa2a1
redhat-bugzilla
=============================================
A race condition flaw was discovered in the Linux kernel's ipc shared memory implimentation. A local user could exploit this flaw to cause a denial of service (system crash) or possibly have unspecied other impacts.
ubuntu
=============================================
Multiple race conditions in ipc/shm.c in the Linux kernel before 3.12.2 allow local users to cause a denial of service (use-after-free and system crash) or possibly have unspecified other impact via a crafted application that uses shmctl IPC_RMID operations in conjunction with other shm system calls.
