A flaw was found in the Linux kernel's ext4 file system. A local user can cause an out-of-bound write in in fs/jbd2/transaction.c code, which can lead to memory corruption. This can mean that the memory can be corrupted to create a denial of service, and a system crash or privilege escalation by unmounting a crafted ext4 filesystem image. References: https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=200069 An upstream patch: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=c37e9e013469521d9adb932d17a1795c139b36db
